{"causes": ["The rise of extreme nationalism and irredentist sentiments in interwar Hungary fostered an environment conducive to ethnic violence.", "Hungary's strategic alliance with Nazi Germany and the Axis powers during World War II provided military and ideological cover for atrocities.", "The perceived need to suppress real or imagined partisan activities in occupied territories led to brutal reprisal policies against civilian populations."], "effects": ["The Novi Sad massacre resulted in the systematic extermination of thousands of Serbian, Jewish, and Romani civilians in January 1942.", "Ferenc Feketehalmy-Czeydner's actions led to his post-war conviction and execution for war crimes and crimes against humanity by a Yugoslav court.", "The massacre left an enduring scar on Hungarian-Yugoslav relations and remains a significant point of historical contention and remembrance."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "novi-sad-massacre", "sourceName": "Novi Sad Massacre", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "ferenc-feketehalmy-czeydner", "targetName": "Ferenc Feketehalmy-Czeydner", "context": "Ferenc Feketehalmy-Czeydner, as a commanding officer, played a leading role in orchestrating the Novi Sad massacre in January 1942."}, {"sourceSlug": "ferenc-feketehalmy-czeydner", "sourceName": "Ferenc Feketehalmy-Czeydner", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "world-war-ii", "targetName": "World War II", "context": "Ferenc Feketehalmy-Czeydner's military career and his involvement in atrocities occurred during the tumultuous period of World War II."}, {"sourceSlug": "ferenc-feketehalmy-czeydner", "sourceName": "Ferenc Feketehalmy-Czeydner", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "novi-sad-massacre", "targetName": "Novi Sad Massacre", "context": "As a commander of the Hungarian V Corps, Ferenc Feketehalmy-Czeydner directly ordered and oversaw the brutal Novi Sad massacre of civilians in January 1942."}, {"sourceSlug": "ferenc-feketehalmy-czeydner", "sourceName": "Ferenc Fekete